<!-- The D. Minn. memorandum's Word styles: the cross-engine recipe (tools/fb/src/docxxengine.rs) in the face of the typst
     template ({font}, Times New Roman) at 13 pt (LR 7.1(h)(1), footnotes too; size 26 half points); Body Text in exact
     29.9 pt line boxes (typst pitch-double, LR 7.1(h)(1) double-spaced) with a half-inch first-line indent; headings,
     block quotations and footnotes in 14.95 pt boxes (typst pitch-single), a heading and a quotation a single line
     from the text on either side, 7 pt between footnotes (typst note-gap); letter page with 1-inch margins and a
     centered page number (LR 5.2(a)), its line 35.45 pt above the page foot (709 twips: where typst sets it,
     footer-descent 30 %). docx/mnd-motion-brief.lua writes the caption, headings, signature and certificate with
     their own spacing. Twips: 20 x pt. -->
<reference xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" base="xengine" size="26" body="598" single="299" indent="720" heading="299" heading-before="299" heading-after="299" quote="299" note-after="140" footer="709"/>
